<td id="A1.F4.sf2.3.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.F4.sf2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12.72" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12.72</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.72</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A1.F4.sf2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Test perplexity</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A1.F4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Streaming synchronization.<span id="A1.F4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Comparison of memory usage and test perplexity with and without streaming synchronization for DiLoCo and our method on a <math id="A1.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math>B-parameter language model trained across <math id="A1.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> nodes.
“By layers” means the <math id="A1.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math> transformer layers are grouped sequentially into <math id="A1.F4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> groups of <math id="A1.F4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, plus a ninth group for embeddings and outer normalization.
“By slices” means synchronization is performed by grouping MLP slices in each layer—<math id="A1.F4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> groups, plus a <math id="A1.F4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>th for embeddings and a <math id="A1.F4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>th for attention and normalization layers.
</span>(a)<span id="A1.F4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Estimated memory usage per GPU (§ <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" title="Memory Usage ‣ 3.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>).
</span>(b)<span id="A1.F4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Final test perplexity after training on <math id="A1.F4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>26</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26</annotation></semantics></math>B tokens.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Parameter Slicing</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our main experiments, we considered two strategies for assigning trainable parameters to each node (§ <a href="#S2.SS2.SSS1" title="2.2.1 Parameter Slicing ‣ 2.2 Partial Parameter Updates ‣ 2 Method ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2.1</span></a>): freezing parts of the MLPs, and freezing MLPs together with a part of attention heads. We also experimented with alternative slicing strategies. For instance, we attempted to slice the outer attention projection <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, but as shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ A.2 Parameter Slicing ‣ Appendix A Ablations ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, this led to some performance degradation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:49%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.22418v1/slicing.svg" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/168;" width="234" height="168"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Test loss as a function of training tokens for different variants of trainable parameter assignment. “By layers” corresponds to training only a subset of layers on each node – slicing model horizontally, whereas “by slices” refers to slicing parameters vertically as described in § <a href="#S2.SS2.SSS1" title="2.2.1 Parameter Slicing ‣ 2.2 Partial Parameter Updates ‣ 2 Method ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2.1</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Another variant we explored was training only a subset of layers on each node. Instead of slicing parameters vertically (by splitting weight matrices into slices), we partitioned the model horizontally, such that each node updates MLP layers parameters within a smaller set of layers. However, this proved to be a significantly harder optimization problem. We were unable to find a hyperparameter configuration that avoided gradient explosion, and training quickly diverged. An example training curve is shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ A.2 Parameter Slicing ‣ Appendix A Ablations ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
It is possible that with more extensive hyperparameter exploration or alternative stabilization techniques, this variant could be made to work, but we leave this for future investigation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Communication Overhead</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider training a <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3</annotation></semantics></math>B-parameter model in bf16, corresponding to <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=2.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=2.6</annotation></semantics></math> GB of gradients, on <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=32</annotation></semantics></math> nodes.
Assume the nodes are connected via a high-speed Wi-Fi 7/8 network with a peak bandwidth of <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=2.875" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.875</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=2.875</annotation></semantics></math> GB/s.
The per-step communication time can be approximated by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{comm}}\approx\frac{2(K-1)}{K}\,\frac{M}{B}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>comm</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{comm}}\approx\frac{2(K-1)}{K}\,\frac{M}{B}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then for DDP:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{comm}}\approx\frac{2(K-1)}{K}\frac{M}{B}\approx 1.75\penalty\ \text{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>comm</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1.75</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{comm}}\approx\frac{2(K-1)}{K}\frac{M}{B}\approx 1.75\penalty\ \text{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This is nearly <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times</annotation></semantics></math> longer than the measured per-step compute time on a single H100 GPU (<math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 0.44\penalty\ \text{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>0.44</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 0.44\penalty\ \text{s}</annotation></semantics></math>), indicating that communication dominates overall step time even under optimistic peak-bandwidth assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, our method and Streaming DiLoCo synchronize only once every <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=100</annotation></semantics></math> steps, reducing the amortized communication cost to</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{low\text{-}comm}}=\frac{T_{\mathrm{comm}}}{S}\approx\frac{1.75}{100}=0.0175\penalty\ \text{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>low</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>comm</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>comm</mi></msub><mi>S</mi></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1.75</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.0175</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{low\text{-}comm}}=\frac{T_{\mathrm{comm}}}{S}\approx\frac{1.75}{100}=0.0175\penalty\ \text{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Convergence Speed Under Bandwidth Constraints ‣ 3.2 Results ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, this substantial reduction in communication time allows our method and Streaming DiLoCo to achieve roughly <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math> faster simulated wall-clock convergence than DDP at Wi-Fi 7 bandwidth, despite requiring more training tokens to reach comparable test loss (44B vs. 26B).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Computational Overhead</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Partial Backward</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MLP with frozen slices</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a single MLP block with up-/down-projection matrices
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{4d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{4d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 4d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 4d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
with an elementwise ReLU in between. Let the input activations for a batch/sequence
be <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> (feature dimension <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> tokens).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We slice the hidden dimension into <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> parts as described in § <a href="#S2.SS2.SSS1" title="2.2.1 Parameter Slicing ‣ 2.2 Partial Parameter Updates ‣ 2 Method ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2.1</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{W}_{1}\\
\vdots\\
\mathbf{W}_{N}\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{W}_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{4d}{N}\times d},\qquad\mathbf{V}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{V}_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\mathbf{V}_{N}\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{V}_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times\frac{4d}{N}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{W}_{1}\\
\vdots\\
\mathbf{W}_{N}\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{W}_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{4d}{N}\times d},\qquad\mathbf{V}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{V}_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;\mathbf{V}_{N}\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{V}_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times\frac{4d}{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define the per-slice pre-activations and activations:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{n}\;=\;\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{4d}{N}\times m},\qquad\mathbf{A}_{n}\;=\;\mathrm{ReLU}(\mathbf{H}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{4d}{N}\times m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{n}\;=\;\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{4d}{N}\times m},\qquad\mathbf{A}_{n}\;=\;\mathrm{ReLU}(\mathbf{H}_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{\frac{4d}{N}\times m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Stacking along the hidden dimension gives
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{H}_{1}\\
\cdots\\
\mathbf{H}_{N}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{4d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{H}_{1}\\
\cdots\\
\mathbf{H}_{N}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{4d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{A}_{1}\\
\cdots\\
\mathbf{A}_{N}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{4d\times m}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{A}_{1}\\
\cdots\\
\mathbf{A}_{N}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{4d\times m}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The MLP forward then decomposes additively over slices:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\;=\;\mathbf{V}\,\mathbf{A}\;=\;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{V}_{n}\mathbf{A}_{n}\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\;=\;\mathbf{V}\,\mathbf{A}\;=\;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{V}_{n}\mathbf{A}_{n}\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Given the upstream gradient <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}=\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}=\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the backward pass:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output projection <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}_{n}}\;=\;\mathbf{G}\mathbf{A}_{n}^{\top},\quad\mathbf{A}_{n}=\mathrm{ReLU}(\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐆𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}_{n}}\;=\;\mathbf{G}\mathbf{A}_{n}^{\top},\quad\mathbf{A}_{n}=\mathrm{ReLU}(\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Activations <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}\;=\;\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}\;=\;\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Through ReLU:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\;=\;\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}\Big)\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0),\quad\mathbf{H}_{n}=\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\;=\;\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}\Big)\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0),\quad\mathbf{H}_{n}=\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Up-projection <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{n}}\;=\;\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\Big)\mathbf{X}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{n}}\;=\;\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\Big)\mathbf{X}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}\;=\;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}\;=\;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">As a result, since we do not update all the slices except <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we do not compute gradients with respect to the frozen weights. This yields FLOP savings, because we skip the multiplications needed to form</p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{n}},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}_{n}},\qquad\forall n\in\{1,\dots,k-1,k+1,\dots,N\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{n}},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}_{n}},\qquad\forall n\in\{1,\dots,k-1,k+1,\dots,N\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Note that we still need to compute the full Jacobian with respect to the input <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\left((\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\left((\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{n}=\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{n}=\mathbf{W}_{n}\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}=\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}=\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Even if the weights of slice <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> are frozen, its contribution
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\big((\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\big((\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
is still required to correctly propagate gradients to earlier layers (see Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MHA with Frozen Heads</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the forward pass of multi-head attention:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{\top}\mathbf{X},\quad\mathbf{K}=\mathbf{W}_{K}^{\top}\mathbf{X},\quad\mathbf{V}=\mathbf{W}_{V}^{\top}\mathbf{X}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{\top}\mathbf{X},\quad\mathbf{K}=\mathbf{W}_{K}^{\top}\mathbf{X},\quad\mathbf{V}=\mathbf{W}_{V}^{\top}\mathbf{X},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{K},\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{hd_{h}\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{K},\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{hd_{h}\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We split them into <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> heads:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{Q}^{(1)}\\
\vdots\\
\mathbf{Q}^{(h)}\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{Q}^{(1)}\\
\vdots\\
\mathbf{Q}^{(h)}\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and similarly for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each head computes</p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{(j)}=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\,\mathbf{Q}^{(j)\top}\mathbf{K}^{(j)},\quad\mathbf{A}^{(j)}=\mathrm{softmax}_{\text{row}}(\mathbf{S}^{(j)}),\quad\mathbf{U}^{(j)}=\mathbf{V}^{(j)}\mathbf{A}^{(j)\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mtext>row</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{(j)}=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\,\mathbf{Q}^{(j)\top}\mathbf{K}^{(j)},\quad\mathbf{A}^{(j)}=\mathrm{softmax}_{\text{row}}(\mathbf{S}^{(j)}),\quad\mathbf{U}^{(j)}=\mathbf{V}^{(j)}\mathbf{A}^{(j)\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Concatenate <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}=[\mathbf{U}^{(1)};\dots;\mathbf{U}^{(h)}]\in\mathbb{R}^{hd_{h}\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}=[\mathbf{U}^{(1)};\dots;\mathbf{U}^{(h)}]\in\mathbb{R}^{hd_{h}\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, then project</p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{W}_{O}^{\top}\mathbf{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{W}_{O}^{\top}\mathbf{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given upstream gradient <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}=\partial\mathcal{L}/\partial\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}=\partial\mathcal{L}/\partial\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output projection.</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{O}}=\mathbf{U}\mathbf{G}^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{U}}=\mathbf{W}_{O}\mathbf{G}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>O</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐔𝐆</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{O}}=\mathbf{U}\mathbf{G}^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{U}}=\mathbf{W}_{O}\mathbf{G}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per head <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{G}_{U}^{(j)}\mathbf{A}^{(j)},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{G}_{U}^{(j)\top}\mathbf{V}^{(j)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{G}_{U}^{(j)}\mathbf{A}^{(j)},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{G}_{U}^{(j)\top}\mathbf{V}^{(j)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Through softmax:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{S}^{(j)}}=\mathrm{softmax}\!\big(\mathbf{A}^{(j)},\,\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}^{(j)}}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.720em;" width="3.720em"><mi>softmax</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{S}^{(j)}}=\mathrm{softmax}\!\big(\mathbf{A}^{(j)},\,\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}^{(j)}}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Back to <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}}=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\,\mathbf{K}^{(j)}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{S}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{K}^{(j)}}=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\,\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{S}^{(j)}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}}=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\,\mathbf{K}^{(j)}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{S}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{K}^{(j)}}=\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\,\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{S}^{(j)}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Back to projection matrices.</span>
Since <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}=\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)\top}\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}=\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)\top}\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{X}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{K}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{X}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{K}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{V}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{X}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{X}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{K}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{X}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{K}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top},\quad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{V}^{(j)}}=\mathbf{X}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}^{(j)}}\Big)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input gradient.</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{j=1}^{h}\Big(\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)}\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}}+\mathbf{W}_{K}^{(j)}\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{K}^{(j)}}+\mathbf{W}_{V}^{(j)}\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}^{(j)}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{j=1}^{h}\Big(\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)}\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Q}^{(j)}}+\mathbf{W}_{K}^{(j)}\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{K}^{(j)}}+\mathbf{W}_{V}^{(j)}\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}^{(j)}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\text{train}}\subseteq\{1,\dots,h\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\text{train}}\subseteq\{1,\dots,h\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of trainable heads on this node (see § <a href="#S2.SS2.SSS1" title="2.2.1 Parameter Slicing ‣ 2.2 Partial Parameter Updates ‣ 2 Method ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2.1</span></a>). Then for all <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\notin\mathcal{H}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\notin\mathcal{H}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)}}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{K}^{(j)}}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{V}^{(j)}}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{Q}^{(j)}}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{K}^{(j)}}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{W}_{V}^{(j)}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Gradients for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{H}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{H}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed as above. Note that the input gradient <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathcal{L}/\partial\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathcal{L}/\partial\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> still aggregates contributions from all heads, so freezing heads saves FLOPs only on parameter gradients computation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>FLOPs calculation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a Transformer with batch size <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, sequence length <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, hidden dimension <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of layers <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, feedforward dimension <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, vocabulary size <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.1 </span>Forward</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The forward FLOPs can be decomposed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Embedding Layer:</span> Although embeddings are typically implemented as lookups with negligible computational cost, for completeness, we estimate the FLOPs as:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{emb}}=B\times S\times H" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>emb</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{emb}}=B\times S\times H</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Head Attention (MHA):</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Linear Projections (Queries, Keys, Values):</p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}=3\times 2\times B\times S\times H\times H=6\times B\times S\times H^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}=3\times 2\times B\times S\times H\times H=6\times B\times S\times H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scaled Dot-Product Attention:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{QK}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{V}}=2\times B\times S^{2}\times H+2\times B\times S^{2}\times H=4\times B\times S^{2}\times H" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>QK</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>V</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{QK}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{V}}=2\times B\times S^{2}\times H+2\times B\times S^{2}\times H=4\times B\times S^{2}\times H</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Output Projection:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out\_proj}}=2\times B\times S\times H\times H" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>out_proj</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out\_proj}}=2\times B\times S\times H\times H</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Total Multi-Head Attention (MHA):</p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>MHA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out\_proj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>out_proj</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out\_proj}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=6\times B\times S\times H^{2}+4\times B\times S^{2}\times H+2\times B\times S\times H^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=6\times B\times S\times H^{2}+4\times B\times S^{2}\times H+2\times B\times S\times H^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=8\times B\times S\times H^{2}+4\times B\times S^{2}\times H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=8\times B\times S\times H^{2}+4\times B\times S^{2}\times H</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feedforward Network (FFN):</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}=2\times 2\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}=4\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>FFN</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}=2\times 2\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}=4\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output projection:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}}=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}_{\text{proj}}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{softmax}}=2\times B\times S\times H\times V+3\times B\times S\times V" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><msub><mtext>out</mtext><mtext>proj</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>softmax</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}}=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}_{\text{proj}}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{softmax}}=2\times B\times S\times H\times V+3\times B\times S\times V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total Forward FLOPs per Layer:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{layer}}=\left(\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}\right)\times L" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>MHA</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>FFN</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{layer}}=\left(\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}\right)\times L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total Forward FLOPs per Step:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{forward}}=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{emb}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{layer}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>forward</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>emb</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{forward}}=\text{FLOPs}_{\text{emb}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{layer}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.2 </span>Backward</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Partial Backward ‣ Appendix C Computational Overhead ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, for the backward computation all slices contribute to the gradients with respect to the input.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MHA backward</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{attn}}=\tfrac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{attn}}=\tfrac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be the trained fraction of heads. Using the forward costs:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}=6\times B\times S\times H^{2},\quad\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}=4\times B\times S^{2}\times H,\quad\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out\_proj}}=2\times B\times S\times H^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>out_proj</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}=6\times B\times S\times H^{2},\quad\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}=4\times B\times S^{2}\times H,\quad\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out\_proj}}=2\times B\times S\times H^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">the backward splits as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(i) Output projection }\mathbf{W}_{O}:\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>(i) Output projection </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>O</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(i) Output projection }\mathbf{W}_{O}:\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{input Jacobian: }2\times B\times S\times H^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>input Jacobian: </mtext><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{input Jacobian: }2\times B\times S\times H^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{parameter gradient: }2\times B\times S\times H^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>parameter gradient: </mtext><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{parameter gradient: }2\times B\times S\times H^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(ii) Attention matmuls (}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top}\text{ and }\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}\text{):}\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(ii) Attention matmuls (</mtext><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mtext> and </mtext><mi>𝐀𝐕</mi><mtext>):</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(ii) Attention matmuls (}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top}\text{ and }\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}\text{):}\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{backward }\approx 2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}=8\times B\times S^{2}\times H," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>backward </mtext><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{backward }\approx 2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{attn}}=8\times B\times S^{2}\times H,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(iii) Q/K/V projections }(\mathbf{W}_{Q},\mathbf{W}_{K},\mathbf{W}_{V}):\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>(iii) Q/K/V projections </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(iii) Q/K/V projections }(\mathbf{W}_{Q},\mathbf{W}_{K},\mathbf{W}_{V}):\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{input Jacobian: }2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}^{\text{(half)}}=6\times B\times S\times H^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>input Jacobian: </mtext><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>(half)</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{input Jacobian: }2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}^{\text{(half)}}=6\times B\times S\times H^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{parameter gradients: }2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}^{\text{(half)}}\times\rho_{\text{attn}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>parameter gradients: </mtext><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>(half)</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{parameter gradients: }2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{proj}}^{\text{(half)}}\times\rho_{\text{attn}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}^{\text{bwd}}=\underbrace{8\times B\times S^{2}\times H}_{\text{attn matmuls}}\;+\;\underbrace{\big(10+6\times\rho_{\text{attn}}\big)\times B\times S\times H^{2}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Q/K/V input Jacobian }(6)\\
\text{+ Q/K/V param grads }(6\rho_{\text{attn}})\\
\text{+ }\mathbf{W}_{O}\text{ input Jacobian }(2)\\
\text{+ }\mathbf{W}_{O}\text{ param grad }(2)\end{subarray}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>MHA</mtext><mtext>bwd</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>attn matmuls</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Q/K/V input Jacobian </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>+ Q/K/V param grads </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>+ </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> input Jacobian </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>+ </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> param grad </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}^{\text{bwd}}=\underbrace{8\times B\times S^{2}\times H}_{\text{attn matmuls}}\;+\;\underbrace{\big(10+6\times\rho_{\text{attn}}\big)\times B\times S\times H^{2}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Q/K/V input Jacobian }(6)\\
\text{+ Q/K/V param grads }(6\rho_{\text{attn}})\\
\text{+ }\mathbf{W}_{O}\text{ input Jacobian }(2)\\
\text{+ }\mathbf{W}_{O}\text{ param grad }(2)\end{subarray}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{attn}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{attn}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (no freezing), this reduces to the usual “backward <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2\times</annotation></semantics></math> forward” for MHA:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}^{\text{bwd}}(\rho_{\text{attn}}{=}1)=8\times B\times S^{2}\times H\;+\;16\times B\times S\times H^{2}\;=\;2\times\big(4\times B\times S^{2}\times H\;+\;8\times B\times S\times H^{2}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>MHA</mtext><mtext>bwd</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mn> 16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mn> 8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}^{\text{bwd}}(\rho_{\text{attn}}{=}1)=8\times B\times S^{2}\times H\;+\;16\times B\times S\times H^{2}\;=\;2\times\big(4\times B\times S^{2}\times H\;+\;8\times B\times S\times H^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">FFN backward</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly as for MHA for FFN let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{mlp}}=\tfrac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>mlp</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{mlp}}=\tfrac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}^{\text{bwd}}=\underbrace{4\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}}_{\text{full input Jacobian}}\;+\;\underbrace{4\times\rho_{\text{mlp}}\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}}_{\text{parameter gradients}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>FFN</mtext><mtext>bwd</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>full input Jacobian</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>mlp</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>parameter gradients</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}^{\text{bwd}}=\underbrace{4\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}}_{\text{full input Jacobian}}\;+\;\underbrace{4\times\rho_{\text{mlp}}\times B\times S\times H\times D_{\text{ff}}}_{\text{parameter gradients}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This results in total backward per step:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FLOPs}_{\text{step}}^{\text{bwd}}=2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{emb}}\;+\;L\times\big(\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}^{\text{bwd}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}^{\text{bwd}}\big)\;+\;2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>step</mtext><mtext>bwd</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>emb</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>MHA</mtext><mtext>bwd</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>FFN</mtext><mtext>bwd</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FLOPs}_{\text{step}}^{\text{bwd}}=2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{emb}}\;+\;L\times\big(\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MHA}}^{\text{bwd}}+\text{FLOPs}_{\text{FFN}}^{\text{bwd}}\big)\;+\;2\times\text{FLOPs}_{\text{out}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Results</h2>

<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:49%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.22418v1/jacobian_dropout.svg" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/170;" width="234" height="170"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A4.F6.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training loss as a function of training tokens for a <math id="A4.F6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="335" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>335</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">335</annotation></semantics></math>M-parameter model
trained with the <math id="A4.F6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math> MLP slicing strategy described in § <a href="#S2.SS2.SSS1" title="2.2.1 Parameter Slicing ‣ 2.2 Partial Parameter Updates ‣ 2 Method ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2.1</span></a>.
<span id="A4.F6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Full Jacobian</span> denotes our standard approach where all slices contribute to the Jacobian.
<math id="A4.F6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.F6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Jacobian</span> corresponds to the detach-all-but-<math id="A4.F6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> variant,
where only the <math id="A4.F6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th slice contributes.
<math id="A4.F6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.F6.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Jacobian</span> refers to the <math id="A4.F6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>+random variant,
where the <math id="A4.F6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th slice and one additional randomly selected slice are retained.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Partial Backward ‣ Appendix C Computational Overhead ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, the only gradients we omit are those with respect to frozen parameters. While this reduces FLOPs during the backward pass, it does not decrease activation memory. A natural question is whether one could go further — not only skipping parameter gradients but also fully detaching their contributions from the gradient flow. We therefore investigated how such a complete detachment of frozen MLP slices affects convergence.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Backward detach-all-but-<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this setting, the forward pass still uses all parameters, but during backpropagation we compute only the Jacobian components corresponding to the active slice.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Backward with zeroed slices (only slice <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> active):</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{A}}_{n}\;=\;\begin{cases}\mathbf{A}_{k},&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{A}}_{n}\;=\;\begin{cases}\mathbf{A}_{k},&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\qquad\widetilde{\mathbf{M}}_{n}\;=\;\begin{cases}\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0),&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\qquad\widetilde{\mathbf{M}}_{n}\;=\;\begin{cases}\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0),&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{n}=\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{n}=\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math> is the elementwise activation mask (e.g., ReLU).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Given upstream <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}=\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}=\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{Y}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}_{n}}=\mathbf{G}\,\widetilde{\mathbf{A}}_{n}^{\top}=\begin{cases}\mathbf{G}\,\mathbf{A}_{k}^{\top},&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{V}_{n}}=\mathbf{G}\,\widetilde{\mathbf{A}}_{n}^{\top}=\begin{cases}\mathbf{G}\,\mathbf{A}_{k}^{\top},&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}=\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G},\qquad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}=\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}\Big)\odot\widetilde{\mathbf{M}}_{n}=\begin{cases}(\mathbf{V}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0),&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}=\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G},\qquad\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}=\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{A}_{n}}\Big)\odot\widetilde{\mathbf{M}}_{n}=\begin{cases}(\mathbf{V}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0),&amp;n=k,\\
\mathbf{0},&amp;n\neq k,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The full-Jacobian input gradient is</p>
<table id="A4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\Big)=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big(\big(\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G}\big)\odot\mathbf{M}_{n}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big(\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}\Big)=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big(\big(\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G}\big)\odot\mathbf{M}_{n}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Under the detach-all-but-<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> rule, this can be written as single-slice contribution:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}\;=\;\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\Big(\big(\mathbf{V}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{G}\big)\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0)\Big)\;}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}\;=\;\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\Big(\big(\mathbf{V}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{G}\big)\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0)\Big)\;}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{H}_{n}}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">As expected, since the full backward pass is disrupted, naively detaching all but one slice resulted in gradient explosion in the middle of training (Figure <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Backward detach-all-but-<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> + random</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To study this further, we considered a variant where, instead of keeping only the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th slice,
we retain the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th slice <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">plus</em> one additional slice chosen at random.
Concretely, during the forward pass we randomly sample an index
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\sim\mathrm{Unif}\big(\{1,\dots,N\}\setminus\{k\}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\sim\mathrm{Unif}\big(\{1,\dots,N\}\setminus\{k\}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
and keep the corresponding contributions in the backward Jacobian.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given the full Jacobian in Eq. <a href="#A4.E1" title="Equation D.1 ‣ Backward detach-all-but-𝑘 ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Partial Parameter Updates for Efficient Distributed Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big((\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbf{W}_{n}^{\top}\Big((\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{n}&gt;0)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">the detach-all-but-<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>+random variant reduces this to</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\Big((\mathbf{V}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\Big((\mathbf{V}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{k}&gt;0)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbf{W}_{g}^{\top}\Big((\mathbf{V}_{g}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{g}&gt;0)\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbf{W}_{g}^{\top}\Big((\mathbf{V}_{g}^{\top}\mathbf{G})\odot\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{H}_{g}&gt;0)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is resampled independently at each step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Despite this modification, performance still degraded (perplexity <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="17.38" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>17.38</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17.38</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16.44" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16.44</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16.44</annotation></semantics></math>). Further investigation of how much of the Jacobian can be dropped could be an interesting direction for future work. Adjusting hyperparameters, or scaling the activations might improve the performance. Also better strategies than picking uniformly at random can be explored.</p>
</div><span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
          
          
          
          
          
          
